<section id="features" class="features section pb-5">
    <div class="container pb-4">
        <div class="row gy-4 align-items-center features-item" style="row-gap: 30px;">
            <div class="col-lg-5  order-1-class justify-content-center flex-column aos-init aos-animate"
                 data-aos="fade-up">
                <h3>Veterinary surgeon</h3>
                <h4 class="mb-3" style="font-size: 19px;">
                    Veterinary costs are one of the biggest costs for a
                    breeder:
                </h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>
                            The cat needs several vaccinations, which often amounts to
                            €25 to €50 per vaccination, depending on which part of the world you live in.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i><span>
                            The cat also needs a chip that varies between €25 and €35 ​​per kitten.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>
                            The cat must also have a rabies vaccination if it goes
                            abroad, which usually costs around €25 and €40 per kitten.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>
                            Many breeders also have their cats neutered or sterilized
                            to prevent litters being created without a contract, which costs €100 to €150 per
                            cat.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>All cats also need a passport 15€ to 30€ per cat.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>
                            ​Deworming must also be given 3 times during the kitten
                            period.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>
                            Often the parents still have to be tested for, for
                            example: FIV/FELV HCM/PKD, but the price varies considerably from breed to breed,
                            depending on the vet, but a test easily costs €100 to €150 per cat.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>There are also people who still do an X-ray.</span></li>
                </ul>

            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-7 order-2-class d-flex align-items-center aos-init aos-animate" data-aos="zoom-out"
                 data-aos-delay="100">
                <div class="image-stack">
                    <img src="~/webassets/images/elements/step-4.jpg" alt="" class="stack-front">
                    <img src="~/webassets/images/elements/step-4.jpg" alt="" class="stack-back">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div><!-- Features Item -->

        <div class="row gy-4 align-items-stretch justify-content-between features-item" style="row-gap: 30px;">
            <div class="col-lg-6 d-flex align-items-center features-img-bg " data-aos="zoom-out">
                <img src="~/webassets/images/elements/step-5.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="">
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5 d-flex justify-content-center flex-column " data-aos="fade-up">
                <h3>Breeding and Nutrition</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>The pedigree must then be requested from the association. Price varies per association.</span></li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i><span>Young cats need a lot of good food to gain weight. Some breeders give their kittens fresh meat, which makes the price even more expensive.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check"></i><span> The mother also needs extra nutrition during pregnancy and feeding the little kittens.</span></li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i><span>
                            The extra cat litter that is used.
                        </span>
                    </li>

                </ul>


            </div>
        </div><!-- Features Item -->

        <div class="row gy-4 align-items-center features-item" style="row-gap: 30px;">
            <div class="col-lg-5  order-1-class justify-content-center flex-column aos-init aos-animate"
                 data-aos="fade-up">
                <h3>Other Costs</h3>

                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>Furthermore, there are other interests that play a role: the kittens you buy are show quality.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <i class="bi bi-check"></i><span>
                            And the bloodlines of the parents and grandparents are of breeding quality.
                        </span>
                    </li>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>Finally, we also have fuel for the car and the time invested in it.</span></li>
                    <li><i class="bi bi-check"></i> <span>So you can imagine that the costs are quite high for a pedigree cat or kitten.</span></li>
                    </li>

                </ul>

            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-7 order-2-class d-flex align-items-center aos-init aos-animate" data-aos="zoom-out"
                 data-aos-delay="100">
